# temps
*~
# emacs auto-save / lock files (a stray #DOD.md# showed up as untracked).
# The leading backslash is required: an unescaped # starts a comment, so a
# pattern like "#*#" is silently ignored by git.
\#*#
.#*

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles
Makefile
cmake_install.cmake
install_manifest.txt

# Build dir

b/
b2/
build/
build_32/
library/docs/public
library/docs/internal
build64/
# Anchored and directory-only on purpose. An unanchored `build*` also matches
# *files* named build* at any depth, which silently swallowed two chapters of
# the cleanup docs (cleanup/findings/build.md, cleanup/plan/build-and-hygiene.md)
# — `git add -A` skipped them and nothing complained. If you add a build tree
# below the repository root, name it here explicitly.
/build*/

